== Trivia==
*Electricity was first detected through electric fish from as far back as 2750 BCE where Ancient Egyptian texts described them as the "protectors" of all other fish. At around 600 BCE, Thales of Miletus made a series of observations on static electricity, from which he believed that friction rendered amber magnetic, in contrast to minerals such as magnetite, which needed no rubbing. Thales was incorrect in believing the attraction was due to a magnetic effect, but later science would prove a link between magnetism and electricity. Electricity would remain little more than an intellectual curiosity for millennia until 1600, when the English scientist William Gilbert wrote ''De Magnete'', in which he made a careful study of electricity and magnetism, distinguishing the lodestone effect from static electricity produced by rubbing amber.
**The Lightning is 1 of 11 [[cards]] associated with electricity, with the others being [[Electro Spirit]], [[Zap]], [[Tesla]], [[Zappies]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Electro Giant]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], [[Wizard Trio]], and the [[Goblinstein]].
***In the Spanish, Korean, Chinese, Malaysian, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Lightning's name translates to "Ray", "Lightning Magic", "Lightning Spell", "Bolt", and "Thunder" respectively.
*The Lightning is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Heal]], [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], [[Rage]], and [[Clone]].
**It resembles the older iteration of the Lightning spell in Clash of Clans that took 2 housing spaces and fired multiple individual strikes. However, unlike the said spell, the Clash Royale iteration fires up to 3 lightning bolts that could stun enemies and only targeted one enemy, whereas its Clash of Clans counterpart fired 6 bolts that could not stun enemies and could deal area damage.
*The Lightning is tied with [[Rocket]] for the most expensive spell, costing 6 [[Elixir]], excluding the [[Mirror]] as it does not have a [[:Category:Variable-Elixir Cards|defined Elixir cost]].
*Although the Lightning has a circular radius, unlike the [[Zap]], it does not inflict area damage. Instead only the highest health troops there are targeted.
*The Lightning, along with the Heal, Freeze, Rage, and [[The Log]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Spells spell] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The [[Ranked|Master 3 League]] badge resembles a Lightning spell bottle.
*The Lightning has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Lightning is 1 of 4 spells that have been featured in the [[Global Spell]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Freeze, and Rage.
***In the Power Surge sub-mode of the Global Spell game mode, the Global Lightning deals more damage than a Lightning card, and can bypass the shields of the [[Royal Recruits]], [[Guards]], and [[Dark Prince]].
**The Lightning is 1 of 5 spells that have been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Spell%20Cauldron|Spell Cauldron]] sub-mode of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Freeze, Rage, and Clone.
*It is 1 of 12 cards that is unavailable in [[Chess Royale]], the others being Royal Recruits, Rocket, Earthquake, Poison, [[Goblin Drill]], [[Miner]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Lightning is the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
*The Lightning was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Lightning was featured in the winning deck of the [https://youtu.be/LWQjS0e6iiE Super Magical Cup Tournament], by a player called CMcHugh.
**The Lightning was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/1fuCnNBTqBU?feature=share King's Cup Tournament], by a player called TMD YAOYAO.
*Before the Lightning's card release, the Lightning's damage was increased by 8%.

